================================================================================================
(1) flat Gaussian toy: exact check of the criterion for two covariance ansaetze
  QUADRATIC V0  (a) Cdot = e^{-tA}        : 1/gamma =     1.6663   gamma =   0.600127   lam_dot(T) = +0.15002
  QUADRATIC V0  (b) Cdot = 1 (T3* ansatz) : 1/gamma =     2.9999   gamma =   0.333344   lam_dot(T) = +0.03000
  FREE V0 = 0   (a) Cdot = e^{-tA}        : 1/gamma =     3.3324   gamma =   0.300082   lam_dot(T) = +0.15000
  FREE V0 = 0   (b) Cdot = 1 (T3* ansatz) : 1/gamma =    29.9990   gamma =   0.033334   lam_dot(T) = +0.00000
  exact answer for (a) with V0 = 0 (PL-POLCHINSKI 6.3): gamma = lam_min(A) = 0.300000
  => the T3* ansatz C_t = t g^{-1} (Cdot = const) gives lam_dot = 1/(t + 1/lam_min)
     for a quadratic V0 (gamma finite) but lam_dot = 0 for the FREE field: in the flat
     case it therefore has no convexification of its own.  On a compact group the
     missing convexification is supplied by Ric/2 = (N/8) g, which is why the group
     criterion survives the free-field test with gamma -> N/8 > 0.

================================================================================================
(2) compact group: the asymptotic value of lam_dot is lam_min(Ric/2) = N/8
  SU(2): lam_dot -> N/8 = 0.2500  (beta-independent, because V_t -> const)
  SU(3): lam_dot -> N/8 = 0.3750  (beta-independent, because V_t -> const)
  SU(4): lam_dot -> N/8 = 0.5000  (beta-independent, because V_t -> const)
  SU(5): lam_dot -> N/8 = 0.6250  (beta-independent, because V_t -> const)

================================================================================================
(3) gamma from a lower bound C and asymptotic rate a
  C=  0.0 T= 1.0 a=0.25:  gamma >= 1.667e-01   (positive for every finite C)
  C=  0.0 T= 5.0 a=0.25:  gamma >= 7.143e-02   (positive for every finite C)

  C=  3.5 T= 1.0 a=0.25:  gamma >= 1.520e-04   (positive for every finite C)
  C=  3.5 T= 5.0 a=0.25:  gamma >= 4.504e-17   (positive for every finite C)

  C= 10.0 T= 1.0 a=0.25:  gamma >= 3.435e-10   (positive for every finite C)
  C= 10.0 T= 5.0 a=0.25:  gamma >= 2.657e-45   (positive for every finite C)

  C= 40.0 T= 1.0 a=0.25:  gamma >= 3.008e-36   (positive for every finite C)
  C= 40.0 T= 5.0 a=0.25:  gamma >= 1.368e-175   (positive for every finite C)

  => (star star) is never the obstruction on a compact group.  The obstruction is
     L-UNIFORMITY of C, and C is controlled by sup|grad S_W|^2, which is EXTENSIVE:
     measured (mc_lattice.log): sum_links |grad S_W|^2 = 900 at L=2 and 14400 at L=4
     (SU(2), beta=2.5) -- a factor 16 for L -> 2L, i.e. exactly L^4, 14.06 per link.
